# Make this crate deterministically testable (dst-rs)

When the user asks to "make this crate deterministically testable" (or
replayable / fault-injectable), follow this playbook. You drive the already-built
`dst-cli` tools (`dst scan`, `dst migrate`) and hand-finish what they skip. Do
**not** write new tooling; do **not** invent CLI flags or `dst-rs` methods.

The binary is `dst` (crate `dst-cli`); in-repo run it as
`cargo run -q -p dst-cli --`.

## Prime rule: the tree compiles at every step

Every step is seam-safe. `dst migrate` adds a `time` field defaulted to the
production clock, so existing callers are unchanged. Migrate one struct at a
time, `cargo check` after each edit, and **prefer a false negative** (leave a
leak, report it) **over a wrong rewrite**. Never commit a red tree.

## Step 1 — Scan

```bash
dst scan --json <path>     # array of {file,line,col,category,snippet,fn}
dst scan <path>            # human summary
```

Categories: `time`, `random`, `network`, `concurrency`. Summarize the counts to
the user. `--deny` turns scan into a non-zero CI gate.

## Step 2 — Ensure dst-rs is a dependency (before migrate)

`dst migrate` runs `cargo check` after rewriting and **auto-restores if it
fails**; the rewrites reference `dst_rs::Time` / `dst_rs::ProductionTime`, so a
crate without the dep produces no change. Add it first:

```bash
cargo add dst-rs --manifest-path <crate>/Cargo.toml          # runtime use
# cargo add dst-rs --dev --manifest-path <crate>/Cargo.toml  # test-only use
```

If dst-rs isn't published, add a path/workspace dependency by hand and confirm
with `cargo check`.

## Step 3 — Migrate the time seams

```bash
dst migrate --dry-run <path>   # unified diff, writes nothing
dst migrate <path>             # applies, then runs cargo check
```

v1 rewrites TIME leaks in inherent methods of named-field structs only: adds
`time: std::sync::Arc<dyn dst_rs::Time>` (defaulted to `dst_rs::ProductionTime`),
and maps `SystemTime::now()…as_millis()` → `self.time.now_ms()`,
`Instant::now()` → `self.time.instant_now()`, `tokio::time::sleep(d).await` →
`self.time.sleep(d).await`. `--traits` accepts only `time` in v1. Report the
migrate summary (structs migrated / leaks rewritten / leaks skipped / check
outcome).

## Step 4 — Hand-finish skipped leaks (same conventions)

- **Free functions**: thread an explicit `time: &dyn dst_rs::Time` param and
  update callers (no `self` to hang a clock off).
- **Random** (`rand::random`, `thread_rng`, `.gen`/`.gen_range`,
  `Uuid::new_v4`, `fastrand`): add `rng: Arc<dyn dst_rs::Random>` defaulted to
  `ProductionRandom`; route via `self.rng.next_u64()` / `next_uuid()` /
  `shuffle_u64()`.
- **Network** (`reqwest`, `TcpStream`, `TcpListener`, tokio net): hide behind a
  trait the test fakes; DST supplies `SimulatedNetwork` + `FaultSchedule`.
- **Concurrency** (`std::thread::spawn`, `tokio::spawn`): route through an
  injected `Executor` (`ProductionExecutor` / `SimulatedExecutor` / `SimScheduler`).

Default every injected field to the production impl. Add a test-only injecting
constructor (e.g. `with_time(tokens, Arc<dyn Time>)`) so tests can pass a
`SimulatedTime`; keep `new` on the production default.

## Step 5 — Scaffold a seed-loop DST test

Model it on `crates/dst-rs/examples/kv_chaos.rs`: inject `SimulatedTime`, loop
seeds, build `FaultSchedule::generate(seed, steps, density)`, step through it,
assert an invariant via `InvariantEngine`. Honor `SEED=<n>` for single-seed
triage. Real API only: `SimulatedTime::new/advance_ms`,
`SimulatedRandom::from_seed/next_u64`, `FaultSchedule::generate/at/fault_steps`,
`Fault::{None,TransientError,CrashRestart,ClockSkew}`,
`InvariantEngine::new/check`, `Invariant::new`, `ddmin`.

## Step 6 — Verify and report

`cargo check` && `cargo test` must be green. Report: what changed, the test
added, and the replay hint `SEED=<n> cargo test <name> -- --nocapture`.
